# Phase 8: A/B kernel slots on the boot disk, with automatic rollback.
@bootdisk
@ai
$ slots
booted slot: a
good slot:   a
next boot:   slot a
$ about
filesystem: BeeFS on ATA disk
$ echo "survives deploys" > /home/bee/note.txt
# A good build: tried in slot b, passes its health check, becomes the good slot.
@deploy
~ \[slots\] trying slot b \(b\d+\): rollback armed, slot a boots next
~ \[disk\] .*partition: BeeFS mounted \(boot #2\)
~ \[slots\] slot b passed its health check: it is now the good slot
$ slots
booted slot: b
good slot:   b
~ ^last trial:  b \(ok, build b\d+\)$
next boot:   slot b
$ log 30
~ "ev":"slot-ok","text":"slot b b\d+ passed its health check"
# A broken build: crashes after arming, so the next boot is slot b again.
@deploy-crash failboot
~ \[slots\] trial of build b\d+ in slot a failed \(crashed or hung\); rolled back to slot b
~ \[crash\] the previous boot crashed .*failboot: simulated broken build
$ slots
booted slot: b
good slot:   b
~ ^last trial:  a \(failed, build b\d+\)$
next boot:   slot b
$ cat /home/bee/note.txt
survives deploys
$ log 40
~ "ev":"rollback","text":"trial of build b\d+ in slot a failed
@signal "kind": "health", "text": "slot b b\d+ passed its health check"
@signal "kind": "crash", "text": "trial of build b\d+ in slot a failed
